{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5048995","formula":"C₃₃H₄₀N₆O₇","hill":"C33H40N6O7","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":33.0,"H":40.0,"N":6.0,"O":7.0},"names":{"en":"Casokefamide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Casokefamide (INN), also known as β-casomorphin 4027 (β-CM-4027) and [D-Ala2,4,Tyr5]-β-casomorphin-5-amide, is a peripherally-specific, synthetic opioid pentapeptide with the amino acid sequence Tyr-D-Ala-Phe-D-Ala-Tyr-NH2. Derived from the β-casomorphin sequence, it was designed with the intention of improving resistance to digestive enzymes so that it could be used as an antidiarrheal medicine. Unlike other casomorphins, which are generally selective μ-opioid receptor agonists, casokefamide binds to both the μ- and δ-opioid receptors."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":5464104,"mass":632.7,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CC1=CC=CC=C1)C(=O)N[C@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC2=CC=C(C=C2)O)C(=O)N)NC(=O)[C@H](CC3=CC=C(C=C3)O)N","inchikey":"XDRHVZLDLNGKLM-FLVVDCEDSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-amino-N-[(2R)-1-[[(2S)-1-[[(2R)-1-[[(2S)-1-amino-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-1-oxopropan-2-yl]amino]-1-oxopropan-2-yl]amino]-1-oxo-3-phenylpropan-2-yl]amino]-1-oxopropan-2-yl]-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"5464104","atoms":86,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.504,"y":-2.076,"z":2.31,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.161,"y":-0.837,"z":1.495,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.637,"y":-0.601,"z":1.498,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.103,"y":0.28,"z":2.176,"el":"O"},{"x":0.079,"y":-1.459,"z":0.707,"el":"N"},{"x":1.529,"y":-1.379,"z":0.538,"el":"C"},{"x":2.303,"y":-2.136,"z":1.629,"el":"C"},{"x":1.859,"y":-3.565,"z":1.847,"el":"C"},{"x":2.301,"y":-4.595,"z":1.007,"el":"C"},{"x":1.867,"y":-5.907,"z":1.207,"el":"C"},{"x":0.992,"y":-6.203,"z":2.249,"el":"C"},{"x":0.549,"y":-5.189